          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Black cake",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "black-cake"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " starts with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "fruit maceration ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "fruit-maceration"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": dried mixed fruit, currants and raisins soaked in rum for at least a week. The fruit absorbs the rum and plumps until almost liquefied, giving the finished cake its characteristic dense, moist texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Molasses gives the cake its dark colour and bitter depth. The batter is blended smooth in the food processor, incorporating the macerated fruit into a very wet mix. Low, slow baking for two hours is what sets it without drying it out."
          }
        ]
      },
